/ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Sudden death due to subarachnoid hemorrhage in case No. 7. An aneurysm in the left middle cerebral artery (arrow) ruptured. Another unruptured aneurysm in the right middle cerebral artery (arrowhead) was observed.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-995-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>The left anterior descending artery (arrow) was completely occluded by a thrombus in case No. 11.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-995-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Fibromuscular dysplasia of the atrioventricular nodal artery in case No. 4. Masson trichrome stain (&#x000d7;100).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-995-g003"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>The clinical characteristics of sudden death related to sexual activity</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-21-995-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>SAH, subarachnoid hemorrhage; MCA, middle cerebral artery; CAD, coronary artery disease; LAD, left anterior descending artery; RCA, right coronary artery; FMD, fibromuscular dysplasia of atrioventricular nodal artery; SEP, steady extramarital partner; 3VD, 3 vessel disease; ACA, anterior communicating artery.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>